================================================================================
Third-party software
================================================================================

goblin-forge is built on the projects below. None of their source is vendored
into this repository — they are fetched by `cargo` and `bun` at build time —
but a compiled Goblin program *does* statically link some of them, so the
distinction between "used to build" and "shipped inside the output" is called
out for each.

Every licence named here is the one the project itself declares. They were read
from the installed packages rather than recalled, but a licence can change
between versions: verify against the exact versions you ship before relying on
this list.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Linked into compiled output
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

These end up inside binaries this compiler produces, which is the case where
attribution obligations follow the artefact rather than the repository.

  Cranelift                       Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
  (cranelift-codegen, -frontend, -module, -native, -object)
  Bytecode Alliance
  https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime
  Code generation. Its output is machine code in every binary produced.

  target-lexicon                  Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
  Bytecode Alliance
  https://github.com/bytecodealliance/target-lexicon

  libc                            MIT OR Apache-2.0
  The Rust Project Developers
  https://github.com/rust-lang/libc
  Used by the Goblin runtime, which is statically linked into every program.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Used to build the compiler
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  TypeScript                      Apache-2.0
  Microsoft Corporation
  https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript
  Not merely a dependency: tsc *is* this compiler's type checker, and its
  verdict on a program is final. See README.

  Bun                             MIT
  Oven
  https://github.com/oven-sh/bun
  The runtime and test runner the compiler's frontend executes under.

  napi-rs                         MIT
  (napi, napi-derive, napi-build)
  https://github.com/napi-rs/napi-rs
  The Node-API boundary between the TypeScript frontend and the Rust backend.

  serde                           MIT OR Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/serde-rs/serde

  postcard, postcard-schema       MIT OR Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/jamesmunns/postcard
  The wire format the MIR crosses the napi boundary in.

  object                          Apache-2.0 OR MIT
  https://github.com/gimli-rs/object
  Object-file writing, beneath cranelift-object.

  anyhow                          MIT OR Apache-2.0
  thiserror                       MIT OR Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/dtolnay/anyhow
  https://github.com/dtolnay/thiserror

  cc                              MIT OR Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/rust-lang/cc-rs

  ts-rs                           MIT
  https://github.com/Aleph-Alpha/ts-rs

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Used to test the compiler
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  CMake                           BSD-3-Clause
  Kitware, Inc. and Contributors
  https://cmake.org
  Drives the differential test suites. It builds the C and C++ oracles that
  this compiler is checked against; neither CMake nor the oracles are part of
  any shipped artefact.

  The platform C and C++ toolchain (MSVC, clang or gcc, whichever CMake finds)
  compiles those oracles. It is whatever is installed on the machine and is not
  distributed with this project.

